text.section:
"Financial corporation" means any corporation not exempted from the imposition of tax under the provisions of § 58.1-401, which derives more than seventy percent of its gross income from the classes of income enumerated in subdivisions 1 through 4 below, without reference to the state wherein such income is earned, including but not limited to small loan companies, sales finance companies, brokerage companies and investment companies:

Fees, commissions, other compensation for financial services rendered;


Gross profits from trading in stocks, bonds, or other securities;


Interest; and


Dividends received to the extent included in Virginia taxable income.
